2026-09-27T12:05:55.8917812Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8918340Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8918661Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8919399Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8920357Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8920459Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8920690Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8921005Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8921324Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8921426Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8921667Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8921818Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8922008Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8922419Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8922658Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8922789Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8923102Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8923307Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8923477Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8923937Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8924365Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8925124Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8925766Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8925890Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8926432Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8927062Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8927384Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8927857Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8938755Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8938973Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8939226Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8939424Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8941017Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8942740Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8943002Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8943573Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8944610Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8945301Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.8945951Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9014349Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9015059Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9015178Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9015489Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9015662Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9016901Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9018243Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9018968Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9019914Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9020130Z 
